15 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Flowchart detailing a dual-branch neural network framework for diabetic retinopathy analysis using a color fundus photograph as input, describing preprocessing, feature extraction, class-balanced and ordinal-risk learning, fusion of probability outputs, and yielding two outputs: five-class severity grading and a referable-risk score for clinical decision-making.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Calibration curve graphic showing two line charts: the left chart titled \215APTOS test\216 and the right chart titled \215Messidor-2.\216 Both plots display observed referable proportion versus mean predicted referable risk, with data points connected and a diagonal dashed reference line representing perfect calibration.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Four confusion matrices compare true versus predicted grades for two datasets and two models. Panel A shows results for the aptos_test dataset with resnet18_ce and ore_mean_all6 models. Panel B shows results for the messidor2_external dataset with resnet18_ce and ore_mean_all6 models. Each matrix uses a blue color gradient representing cell value magnitude, with axes labeled true grade and predicted grade, and prominent diagonal values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side confusion matrices comparing DR grade prediction methods, with Argmax prediction on the left and validation-calibrated thresholds on the right. Each matrix displays true versus predicted DR grades from zero to four, with color intensity reflecting the mean image count and a color bar legend included.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Four-panel figure comparing retinal fundus photographs and corresponding Grad-CAM overlays for two cases labeled A and B. Each case includes an original retinal image on the left showing typical orange coloration and vascular structures, and a Grad-CAM heatmap overlay on the right highlighting regions of interest in red and yellow, indicating high model attention. Both cases are annotated as true grade three with a predicted referable risk score of one point zero zero.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
